, BTO\ndescription: Indicates tissue/organ is the primary experimental variable.\ninstructions: Return the tissue/organ name if different tissues are compared.\n  Otherwise return null.\n\nterm: factor value time\nsdrf_column: factor value[time]\nontology: EFO:0000721\ndescription: Indicates time point is the primary experimental variable.\npattern: number + time unit\ninstructions: Return the time points compared if a time-course experiment.\n  Otherwise return null.\n\nterm: factor value treatment\nsdrf_column: factor value[treatment]\nontology: EFO:0000727, NCIT, EFO\ndescription: Indicates treatment/perturbation is the primary experimental variable.\ninstructions: Return the treatment type if different treatments are compared\n  (e.g. different growth conditions, carbon sources, stress conditions).\n  Otherwise return null.\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nReturn a single JSON object where each key is the exact sdrf_column string shown above.\nFor each key, return a dict with:\n  "value": the extracted value (string or null — null if this variable is not\n           the primary experimental factor in this study)\n  "accession": ontology accession if resolvable, else null\n  "confidence": "high", "medium", or "low"\n  "evidence_quote": short verbatim quote from the text, or null\n  "evidence_location": location in the paper (e.g. "Abstract", "Methods"), or null\n\nNote: Most XL-MS datasets will have only one or two non-null factor values.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '[TITLE]\nStreptavidin biotin-CCW16 pulldown to determine CCW16-modified proteins in HeLa lysate\n\n[ABSTRACT]\nThe SUMO-targeted E3 ubiquitin ligase RNF4 plays an important role in safeguarding genome and proteome integrity. RNF4 recognizes polySUMO modified proteins and induces their proteolytic or non-proteolytic ubiquitylation. Based on the key functions of RNF4 maintaining proteome and genome stability, control of DNA damage response and DNA-pro